<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22187" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnānĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		inanis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>emptiness</i>, <i>empty space</i> (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mihi inanitate Jamdudum intestina murmurant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Cas. 4, 3, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per inanitatem ferri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fat. 9, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 11, 6</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>emptiness</i>, <i>uselessness</i>, <i>inanity</i> (rare
			but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amputata circumcisaque inanitate omni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 1, 13, 44</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc. 3, 2, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verborum et imaginum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					13, 8, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
